The Kernel type is likely in the SemanticKernel.Core project, but I don't see Kernel.cs directly. It might be in the AI or Functions subfolders or in KernelExtensions.cs. Since Kernel is sealed, I cannot subclass it for testing. Also, the extension method uses the logger from kernel.LoggerFactory to create a logger instance.

I will write a test that creates a real Kernel instance (if possible) or mocks the ILoggerFactory and ILogger to verify the LogWarning calls. Since the extension method is static and uses the logger created from kernel.LoggerFactory, I can mock the LoggerFactory to return a mock ILogger that records the LogWarning calls.

I will submit a test that mocks ILoggerFactory and ILogger, sets up a Kernel with the mocked LoggerFactory, and calls the extension method with a crafted manifest file that triggers the LogWarning calls on line 114 and the other warning on line 108.

I will create a minimal manifest file content to trigger the "No functions found in the runtime object." and "No API description URL found in the runtime object." warnings.

I will submit the test now.

